{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525884-how-compatible-is-2ed-to-1ed","id":525884,"title":"how compatible is 2ed to 1ed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-23T14:05:58-07:00","id":525884,"title":"how compatible is 2ed to 1ed?","content":"Do I buy 2ed? Thing is my players all have copies of 1ed and if I buy 2ed I will likely be the only one (money sucks), so if I convert over will they still be able to get mileage out of their books or am I telling them to shelve their copies and fight over mine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:12:28-07:00","id":525905,"title":"","content":"They'll want to have access to the player section of the book, for advancement. Mainly the third chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:20:07-07:00","id":525917,"title":"","content":"There's a fairly big &quot;it depends,&quot; that's going to happen here. Some 1e material is going to do just fine with 2e (at least until it gets 2e treatment). Other things aren't.<br /> <br /> In general: Non-mechanical heavy mortal stuff will work fine. Some mechanical tweaking might happen (esp. stuff that should be Conditions), but in general this isn't a problem. Most of the mechanics heavy mortal stuff is covered in the GMC-RU free document (also something that can help alleviate everyone fighting over one copy of the core book). Werewolf specific stuff is going to be much less useful. Some of the bigger picture stuff hasn't changed, but lots of things are different. You can't rely on the WtF 1e core book for things like form bonuses, Gifts, Auspice powers, Harmony, Renown, Rituals, Wolf-blooded... all those things have had major revisions,<br /> <br /> So, yeah, for the werewolf specific stuff, you're a pretty much stuck with 2e at the moment. Some of the 1e supplements have material that's useful, but for the most part it'll be the exception. Lodges are probably the thing that transfer over the easiest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:21:35-07:00","id":525918,"title":"","content":"It's pretty easy to port mechanics back and forth, but all the players will probably need access to the 2e core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T15:48:48-07:00","id":526035,"title":"","content":"In terms of compatibility? That's a long answer that mixes yes and no together. There's a lot of first edition material that still works as is or nearly as such. Stuff that doesn't hook into the unique mechanics of werewolves, especially, is pretty easy.<br /> <br /> In terms of your players not having their own copy and fighting over yours? That is definitely going to happen, second edition changes the rules and adds important new rules that players are going to want to have access to. It won't necessarily invalidate stuff in supplements they own, but the 1e corebook is entirely insufficient for playing a 2e werewolf unless you're in the habit of having your players go purely by the fluff and handling all the mechanics yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}